SUMMARY:Spirited Improv Community Playshop
DESCRIPTION:Awakening Asheville\nThis is not traditional improvisation. Im
 agine Spirited Improv as a spiritual practice\, where creativity meets con
 sciousness and community. No experience necessary.\n\n**ABOUT SPIRITED IMP
 ROV**\nSpirited Improv is a unique fusion of expressive arts\, spiritual p
 ractice\, and group play that helps you release fear\, trust the unknown\,
  and show up as your truest self.\nSpirited Improv is a soul-centered comm
 unity experience that uses improvisational play as the container for spiri
 tual growth\, personal transformation\, and authentic connection. Rather t
 han focusing on comedy or performance\, we use improv as a living practice
 \, one that invites presence\, trust\, curiosity\, and responsiveness in t
 he moment.\n\nFacilitated by Jessica Chilton\, who brings over 20 years of
  improvisational performing arts experience and 16 years as an expressive 
 arts therapist\, weaving creativity\, spirituality\, and presence into a s
 afe\, transformative group experience.\n\n**2 HR COMMUNITY PLAYSHOP**\nThi
 s special session takes place on the final day of the current Spirited Imp
 rov series\, when we open the experience to the wider community.\nYou’ll
  join the participants who have been playing together throughout the serie
 s. You’re welcome to watch from the audience and enjoy the unfolding exp
 erience\, or jump in and participate in the improvisational play alongside
  the group.\nGreat opportunity to try it out before joining a multi-week s
 eries.\n\n**WHAT PAST PARTICIPANTS ARE SAYING**\n\n“Spirited Improv is a
 uthentic\, vulnerable and connective. It meets my need to deeply feel\, be
  seen and see others. On my first night I experienced such a profound heal
 ing experience after sharing what was on my heart. It was like a sound\, h
 ealing touch\, full moon energy bath that opened my heart. ” \\~ Kate\n\
 n“Spirited Improv is a fun and little bit edgy way of interacting with t
 he mystery of the moment. You decide how much you want to interact or obse
 rve from the audience so you never have to do anything you don't want to d
 o. It is an opportunity to let go of control and explore the spontaneity o
 f life and creativity in a supportive\, safe environment..” \\~ Kenyon\n
 \n“I got to play\, move my body\, laugh\, take joy in watching my friend
 s come alive\, give and receive big hugs\, and feel the presence of the an
 cestors who always join me. There’s something so sacred about being pres
 ent with others while we play\, witness and embody what is.” \\~ Sue\n\n
 PAY WHAT YOU WANT OPTION $1 - $50\nMore info at [https://spiritedimprov.co
 m](https://spiritedimprov.com/)
